IMPORT prelude

-- Local Government Act 1993 (NSW), Chapter 15, Part 8, Division 1 (ss 575-584) -- concessions for pensioners, with
-- the Local Government (General) Regulation 2021, Part 5, Division 4 (cll 134-136), which prescribes who is an
-- eligible pensioner.
--
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. The rules are written in the Act's own actors and terms: "an eligible pensioner", "a jointly
-- eligible occupier", "the person making the application", "the council". The pensioner's questions are in
-- lga-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module and restates no rule. The council is a public body: its duties are
-- regulative rules here, with the council as the actor, but it gets no seat.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Dictionary: "dwelling", "eligible pensioner", "jointly eligible occupier", "quarter", "year".
-- s 575(1)-(5) (the reduction, its amount, the caps, becoming a pensioner after the levy, discharge between joint
-- liables); s 576 (postponed rates, as an instruction for the amount entered); s 579 with cl 135 (the application);
-- s 583 (writing off; no recovery); s 584 (ending of the concession; the credit); s 582 with cl 136 (who the council
-- may choose to relieve, as a permission). Not covered, with an explicit answer: a s 580 regulation varying the
-- amounts, a ss 577-578 hardship order, a s 582 waiver's amount.
--
-- EDITION. Act: act-1993-030, version 2025-01-01; Regulation: sl-2021-0460, version 2024-09-02; both from the Open
-- Australian Legal Corpus as collected on 10 March 2025, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/act-1993-030.txt and
-- ../../../local-government-general-regulation-2021/registers/source-bundle/sl-2021-0460.txt.
-- NOT THE CURRENT OFFICIAL TEXT AND MAY BE OUT OF DATE: check legislation.nsw.gov.au before relying on it.
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (CC BY 4.0).
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Local Government Act 1993 (NSW), ss 575-584 -- concessions for pensioners: seat-neutral core`

§§ `cl 134 -- the classes prescribed for the definition of eligible pensioner`

-- Dictionary, "eligible pensioner", para (a): "who is a member of a class of persons prescribed by the regulations".
-- Regulation cl 134 prescribes five classes. Every fact below is a Commonwealth status, asked as a fact (a borrowed
-- term): the Social Security Act 1991, the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 and the Military Rehabilitation and
-- Compensation Act 2004 decide them, and NOTES.md says which Commonwealth encodings answer which.
DECLARE `Commonwealth payments and card` HAS
    -- cl 134(a): "a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991 of the Commonwealth"
    `receives a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 134(a): "or a service pension under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 of the Commonwealth"
    `receives a service pension under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 134(a): "and who are entitled to a pensioner concession card issued by or on behalf of the Commonwealth
    -- Government"
    `is entitled to a pensioner concession card` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 134(b)(i): "a pension from the Commonwealth Department of Veterans' Affairs as ... a war widow or war widower
    -- within the meaning of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986"
    `receives a DVA pension as a war widow or war widower` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 134(b)(ii), (iii): "the unmarried mother" or "the widowed mother of a deceased unmarried member of the
    -- Australian Defence or Peacekeeping Forces"
    `receives a DVA pension as the unmarried or widowed mother of a deceased unmarried member of the Defence or Peacekeeping Forces` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 134(b1): "have received a lump sum mentioned in section 234(1)(b) of the Military Rehabilitation and
    -- Compensation Act 2004 ... or are receiving a weekly amount mentioned in that paragraph"
    `has received the MRCA s 234(1)(b) lump sum or receives the weekly amount` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 134(b), (b1): "and do not have income and assets that would prevent them from being granted a pensioner
    -- concession card (assuming they were eligible for such a card)"
    `has income and assets that would not prevent the grant of a pensioner concession card` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 134(c): "a general rate of pension adjusted for extreme disablement under section 22(4) of the Veterans'
    -- Entitlements Act 1986 ..., or a special rate of pension under section 24 of that Act"
    `receives the VEA s 22(4) extreme disablement rate or the s 24 special rate` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 134(d): "receive, or who at some point in their life have been eligible for, a Special Rate Disability Pension
    -- under the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004"
    `receives, or has at some time been eligible for, the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Prescribed class` IS ONE OF
    `cl 134(a): a Social Security Act Chapter 2 pension, benefit or allowance, or a VEA Part III service pension, with entitlement to a pensioner concession card`
    `cl 134(b): a DVA pension as a war widow or widower, or as the mother of a deceased unmarried member, within the pensioner concession card income and assets limits`
    `cl 134(b1): an MRCA s 234(1)(b) lump sum or weekly amount, within the pensioner concession card income and assets limits`
    `cl 134(c): the VEA s 22(4) extreme disablement rate or the s 24 special rate`
    `cl 134(d): the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension, received now or eligible for at some time`
    `in no class prescribed by cl 134`

-- The first class (in the clause's order) whose conditions are met. A person may be in more than one; one is enough.
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Commonwealth payments and card`
GIVETH A `Prescribed class`
`the cl 134 class of` `the person` MEANS
    IF      (    `the person`'s `receives a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991`
             OR  `the person`'s `receives a service pension under Part III of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986`)
        AND `the person`'s `is entitled to a pensioner concession card`
    THEN `cl 134(a): a Social Security Act Chapter 2 pension, benefit or allowance, or a VEA Part III service pension, with entitlement to a pensioner concession card`
    ELSE IF     (    `the person`'s `receives a DVA pension as a war widow or war widower`
                 OR  `the person`'s `receives a DVA pension as the unmarried or widowed mother of a deceased unmarried member of the Defence or Peacekeeping Forces`)
            AND `the person`'s `has income and assets that would not prevent the grant of a pensioner concession card`
         THEN `cl 134(b): a DVA pension as a war widow or widower, or as the mother of a deceased unmarried member, within the pensioner concession card income and assets limits`
         ELSE IF     `the person`'s `has received the MRCA s 234(1)(b) lump sum or receives the weekly amount`
                 AND `the person`'s `has income and assets that would not prevent the grant of a pensioner concession card`
              THEN `cl 134(b1): an MRCA s 234(1)(b) lump sum or weekly amount, within the pensioner concession card income and assets limits`
              ELSE IF `the person`'s `receives the VEA s 22(4) extreme disablement rate or the s 24 special rate`
                   THEN `cl 134(c): the VEA s 22(4) extreme disablement rate or the s 24 special rate`
                   ELSE IF `the person`'s `receives, or has at some time been eligible for, the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension`
                        THEN `cl 134(d): the MRCA Special Rate Disability Pension, received now or eligible for at some time`
                        ELSE `in no class prescribed by cl 134`

GIVEN `the class` IS A `Prescribed class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a prescribed class` `the class` IF
    CONSIDER `the class`
    WHEN `in no class prescribed by cl 134` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Dictionary -- eligible pensioner and dwelling`

-- Dictionary: "eligible pensioner, in Division 1 of Part 8 of Chapter 15, in relation to a rate or charge levied on
-- land on which a dwelling is situated means a person-- (a) who is a member of a class of persons prescribed by the
-- regulations, and (b) who occupies that dwelling as his or her sole or principal place of living."
-- "dwelling, in Division 1 of Part 8 of Chapter 15, means a building or part of a building used as a place of
-- dwelling." Both facts are about the land the rate or charge is levied on.
DECLARE `Occupation of the land` HAS
    `a dwelling is situated on the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `occupies that dwelling as sole or principal place of living` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Eligible pensioner answer` IS ONE OF
    `an eligible pensioner for the rates and charges on this land` HAS `the class` IS A `Prescribed class`
    `not an eligible pensioner: in no class prescribed by cl 134`
    `not an eligible pensioner: no dwelling (a building or part of one used as a place of dwelling) is situated on the land`
    `not an eligible pensioner: does not occupy the dwelling as sole or principal place of living`

GIVEN `the person`     IS A `Commonwealth payments and card`
      `the occupation` IS AN `Occupation of the land`
GIVETH AN `Eligible pensioner answer`
`the eligible pensioner status of` `the person` `on` `the occupation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`is a prescribed class` (`the cl 134 class of` `the person`))
    THEN `not an eligible pensioner: in no class prescribed by cl 134`
    ELSE IF NOT (`the occupation`'s `a dwelling is situated on the land`)
         THEN `not an eligible pensioner: no dwelling (a building or part of one used as a place of dwelling) is situated on the land`
         ELSE IF NOT (`the occupation`'s `occupies that dwelling as sole or principal place of living`)
              THEN `not an eligible pensioner: does not occupy the dwelling as sole or principal place of living`
              ELSE `an eligible pensioner for the rates and charges on this land` (`the cl 134 class of` `the person`)

GIVEN `the answer` IS AN `Eligible pensioner answer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `says eligible pensioner` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `an eligible pensioner for the rates and charges on this land` `c` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Dictionary -- jointly eligible occupier`

-- Dictionary: "jointly eligible occupier, in Division 1 of Part 8 of Chapter 15, in relation to a rate or charge in
-- respect of which an eligible pensioner is jointly liable, means a person who-- (a) is the spouse or de facto
-- partner of that eligible pensioner, or (b) is another eligible pensioner, or (c) if another eligible pensioner and
-- his or her spouse or de facto partner have the same sole or principal place of dwelling, is the spouse or de facto
-- partner of that other eligible pensioner, and whose sole or principal place of living is the same as that of that
-- firstmentioned eligible pensioner."
-- One record for each other person jointly liable with the eligible pensioner (s 560(3): joint owners are jointly and
-- severally liable).
DECLARE `Other person liable` HAS
    `is the spouse or de facto partner of the eligible pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is another eligible pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner who has the same sole or principal place of dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the same sole or principal place of living as the eligible pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the other person` IS AN `Other person liable`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a jointly eligible occupier` `the other person` IF
        (    `the other person`'s `is the spouse or de facto partner of the eligible pensioner`
         OR  `the other person`'s `is another eligible pensioner`
         OR  `the other person`'s `is the spouse or de facto partner of another eligible pensioner who has the same sole or principal place of dwelling`)
    AND `the other person`'s `has the same sole or principal place of living as the eligible pensioner`

§§ `s 575(1), (2) -- who is liable, and which paragraph applies`

-- s 575(1): "If an eligible pensioner is the person solely liable, or a person jointly liable with one or more other
-- persons, for a rate or charge levied on land on which a dwelling is situated, the rate or charge is, on application
-- to the council and on production to the council of evidence sufficient to enable it to calculate the amount of the
-- reduction, to be reduced in accordance with this section."
-- An empty list of other persons is "solely liable". The part liable as between all persons is a fraction of the whole
-- (for example 0.5); it is read only under s 575(2)(b).
DECLARE `Liability for the rates` HAS
    `the other persons liable` IS A LIST OF `Other person liable`
    `the part for which the applicant and any jointly eligible occupier are liable, as between all persons liable` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `s 575(2) paragraph` IS ONE OF
    `s 575(2)(a): solely liable, or jointly liable with jointly eligible occupiers and no other person -- one-half`
    `s 575(2)(b): jointly liable with a person who is not a jointly eligible occupier -- the proportional share of one-half`

-- s 575(2)(a): "solely liable or jointly liable with one or more jointly eligible occupiers but with no other person";
-- (b): "jointly liable with one other person who is not a jointly eligible occupier, or with two or more other
-- persons, any of whom is not a jointly eligible occupier". Together: (b) if any other person liable is not a jointly
-- eligible occupier; otherwise (a).
GIVEN `the liability` IS A `Liability for the rates`
GIVETH A `s 575(2) paragraph`
`the s 575(2) paragraph for` `the liability` MEANS
    IF all (GIVEN `p` YIELD `is a jointly eligible occupier` `p`) (`the liability`'s `the other persons liable`)
    THEN `s 575(2)(a): solely liable, or jointly liable with jointly eligible occupiers and no other person -- one-half`
    ELSE `s 575(2)(b): jointly liable with a person who is not a jointly eligible occupier -- the proportional share of one-half`

-- s 575(2)(b): "an amount that bears to one-half of the rate or charge the same proportion as the part of that rate
-- or charge for which, as between all persons liable to pay the rate or charge, the applicant and any jointly eligible
-- occupier are liable bears to the whole of that rate or charge." Under (a) the proportion is the whole (1).
GIVEN `the liability` IS A `Liability for the rates`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 575(2) proportion for` `the liability` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the s 575(2) paragraph for` `the liability`
    WHEN `s 575(2)(a): solely liable, or jointly liable with jointly eligible occupiers and no other person -- one-half` THEN 1
    WHEN `s 575(2)(b): jointly liable with a person who is not a jointly eligible occupier -- the proportional share of one-half` THEN `the liability`'s `the part for which the applicant and any jointly eligible occupier are liable, as between all persons liable`

-- The share is a part of the whole: more than nothing and at most all of it. Outside that, the answer is not covered.
GIVEN `the liability` IS A `Liability for the rates`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stated part is a part of the whole` `the liability` IF
        `the liability`'s `the part for which the applicant and any jointly eligible occupier are liable, as between all persons liable` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the liability`'s `the part for which the applicant and any jointly eligible occupier are liable, as between all persons liable` AT MOST 1

GIVEN `the liability` IS A `Liability for the rates`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is jointly liable` `the liability` IF
    NOT (null (`the liability`'s `the other persons liable`))

§§ `s 575(2), (3) -- the amount of the reduction for the year`

-- The rates and charges levied on the land for one year ("year means the period from 1 July to the following 30
-- June"), grouped as s 575(3) groups them. s 576: "If the payment of part of a rate which is required to be reduced
-- by section 575 is postponed under Division 2, the amount of the rate for the purposes of this Division is taken to
-- be the amount of that part of the rate that is not postponed" -- so the amounts are the parts not postponed.
-- `other rates or charges`: any other rate or charge levied on the land (another special rate, a stormwater
-- management services charge): s 575(1) and (2) reach "a rate or charge"; s 575(3) caps only the three groups.
-- READING (finding 3): the text halves such a rate or charge with no cap.
DECLARE `Rates and charges levied for the year` HAS
    `ordinary rates` IS A NUMBER
    `domestic waste management charges` IS A NUMBER
    `water supply special rates or charges` IS A NUMBER
    `sewerage special rates or charges` IS A NUMBER
    `other rates or charges` IS A NUMBER

-- s 575(3): "The total amount by which-- (a) all ordinary rates and charges for domestic waste management services
-- levied on any land for the same year are reduced is not to exceed $250, and (b) all water supply special rates or
-- charges so levied are reduced is not to exceed $87.50, and (c) all sewerage special rates or charges so levied are
-- reduced is not to exceed $87.50. However, if subsection (2)(b) applies, the maximum amounts specified in this
-- subsection are to be proportionately reduced in line with the proportion applicable under subsection (2)(b)."
-- s 580 lets a regulation vary these; the deposited regulation does not.
`the s 575(3)(a) cap` MEANS 250
`the s 575(3)(b) cap` MEANS 87.5
`the s 575(3)(c) cap` MEANS 87.5
`one-half` MEANS 0.5

DECLARE `Reduction` HAS
    `on ordinary rates and domestic waste management charges` IS A NUMBER
    `on water supply special rates or charges` IS A NUMBER
    `on sewerage special rates or charges` IS A NUMBER
    `on other rates or charges` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the reduction` IS A `Reduction`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total of` `the reduction` MEANS
      `the reduction`'s `on ordinary rates and domestic waste management charges`
    PLUS `the reduction`'s `on water supply special rates or charges`
    PLUS `the reduction`'s `on sewerage special rates or charges`
    PLUS `the reduction`'s `on other rates or charges`

-- One group: one-half of the group times the proportion, but not more than the cap times the proportion.
GIVEN `the amount levied` IS A NUMBER
      `the cap`           IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the capped reduction of` `the amount levied` `under` `the cap` `at` `the proportion` MEANS
    min ((`one-half` TIMES `the amount levied`) TIMES `the proportion`) (`the cap` TIMES `the proportion`)

-- s 575(2) and (3), for a person who was an eligible pensioner on the day the rate or charge was levied.
GIVEN `the rates`      IS A `Rates and charges levied for the year`
      `the proportion` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Reduction`
`the s 575(2) and (3) reduction of` `the rates` `at` `the proportion` MEANS
    `Reduction` WITH
        `on ordinary rates and domestic waste management charges` IS `the capped reduction of` (`the rates`'s `ordinary rates` PLUS `the rates`'s `domestic waste management charges`) `under` `the s 575(3)(a) cap` `at` `the proportion`
        `on water supply special rates or charges`                IS `the capped reduction of` (`the rates`'s `water supply special rates or charges`) `under` `the s 575(3)(b) cap` `at` `the proportion`
        `on sewerage special rates or charges`                    IS `the capped reduction of` (`the rates`'s `sewerage special rates or charges`) `under` `the s 575(3)(c) cap` `at` `the proportion`
        `on other rates or charges`                               IS (`one-half` TIMES (`the rates`'s `other rates or charges`)) TIMES `the proportion`

§§ `Dictionary "quarter" -- counting quarters of the year`

-- Dictionary: "quarter means a period of 3 months ending on 30 September, 31 December, 31 March or 30 June"; "year
-- means the period from 1 July to the following 30 June". The rating year is named by the calendar year in which it
-- starts (2025 for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026).
GIVEN `the rating year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the first days of the quarters of` `the rating year` MEANS
    LIST DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 `the rating year`),
         DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 `the rating year`),
         DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 (`the rating year` PLUS 1)),
         DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 4 (`the rating year` PLUS 1))

-- "full quarters remaining after the day": a quarter is full and remaining after a day if it begins after that day.
GIVEN `the rating year` IS A NUMBER
      `the day`         IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of full quarters of` `the rating year` `remaining after` `the day` MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN `first day` YIELD `first day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the day`) (`the first days of the quarters of` `the rating year`))

GIVEN `the day`         IS A DATE
      `the rating year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls in the rating year` `the day` `the rating year` IF
        DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 `the rating year`)
    AND DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT MOST  DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 (`the rating year` PLUS 1))

-- The rating year a day falls in.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rating year containing` `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` AT LEAST 7
    THEN DATE_YEAR `the day`
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS 1

§§ `s 575(2), (4) -- eligible on the levy day, or later`

-- s 575(2): the person making the application is, "on the date on which the rate or charge is levied, an eligible
-- pensioner". s 575(4): "If a person becomes an eligible pensioner after the day on which a rate or charge is made and
-- levied, the person is entitled to a reduction under this section of the rate or charge proportionate to the number
-- of full quarters remaining after the day on which the person becomes an eligible pensioner in the year for which
-- the rate or charge is made." s 546(1): "A rate or charge is levied on the land specified in a rates and charges
-- notice by the service of the notice"; (2) the notice may be served after 1 July in the year "or in a subsequent
-- year". A notice served outside the rating year it is for is not covered.
DECLARE `s 575(4) position` IS ONE OF
    `the whole year: an eligible pensioner on the day the rate or charge was levied (s 575(2))`
    `full quarters remaining after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))` HAS `full quarters` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: the rates notice was not served in the rating year it is for (s 546(2), (3))`

GIVEN `the rating year`                  IS A NUMBER
      `the levy day`                     IS A DATE
      `the day of becoming an eligible pensioner` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 575(4) position`
`the s 575(4) position for` `the rating year` `levied on` `the levy day` `eligible from` `the day of becoming an eligible pensioner` MEANS
    IF NOT (`falls in the rating year` `the levy day` `the rating year`)
    THEN `not covered: the rates notice was not served in the rating year it is for (s 546(2), (3))`
    ELSE IF DATE_SERIAL `the day of becoming an eligible pensioner` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the levy day`
         THEN `the whole year: an eligible pensioner on the day the rate or charge was levied (s 575(2))`
         ELSE `full quarters remaining after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))` (`the number of full quarters of` `the rating year` `remaining after` `the day of becoming an eligible pensioner`)

-- READING (finding 4): "a reduction under this section ... proportionate to the number of full quarters" is the
-- reduction s 575(2) and (3) would give, caps included, times the full quarters over the four quarters of the year.
GIVEN `the reduction` IS A `Reduction`
      `the fraction`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Reduction`
`the reduction` `scaled by` `the fraction` MEANS
    `Reduction` WITH
        `on ordinary rates and domestic waste management charges` IS `the reduction`'s `on ordinary rates and domestic waste management charges` TIMES `the fraction`
        `on water supply special rates or charges`                IS `the reduction`'s `on water supply special rates or charges` TIMES `the fraction`
        `on sewerage special rates or charges`                    IS `the reduction`'s `on sewerage special rates or charges` TIMES `the fraction`
        `on other rates or charges`                               IS `the reduction`'s `on other rates or charges` TIMES `the fraction`

`the number of quarters in a year` MEANS 4

§§ `s 575 -- the reduction, or why there is none`

-- Not covered, each with the reason. s 580: "The amount by which a rate or charge is to be reduced in accordance with
-- this Division may be varied from time to time by the regulations" (the deposited regulation varies nothing). s 577:
-- a council "may, by order", to avoid hardship, treat a co-occupier as an eligible pensioner, or a pensioner who pays
-- the whole as solely liable; s 578: the order's effective date, and directions on refunds and interest "as the
-- council thinks fit". s 582: "A council may waive or reduce rates, charges and interest due by any person prescribed
-- by the regulations" (cl 136). Each is a council discretion; the order or waiver is taken as a fact, and the answer
-- is not covered.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `a regulation under s 580 varies the amounts of the reduction; the deposited regulation varies none`
    `a council hardship order under ss 577 and 578 applies; its effect and date are the council's`
    `a council waiver or reduction under s 582 and cl 136 applies; its amount is the council's`
    `the rates notice was not served in the rating year it is for (s 546(2), (3))`
    `the part stated for the applicant and jointly eligible occupiers is not more than 0 and at most 1`

DECLARE `Reduction answer` IS ONE OF
    `on application with evidence, reduced by (dollars)` HAS `the reduction` IS A `Reduction`
                                                             `in all`        IS A NUMBER
    `no reduction: not an eligible pensioner` HAS `because` IS AN `Eligible pensioner answer`
    `no reduction this year: no full quarter of the rating year remained after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))`
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

-- Council relief taken as facts (each makes the answer not covered).
DECLARE `Council relief and regulations` HAS
    `a regulation under s 580 varies the amounts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a council hardship order under s 577 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a council waiver or reduction under s 582 applies` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the reduction` IS A `Reduction`
GIVETH A `Reduction answer`
`reduced by` `the reduction` MEANS
    `on application with evidence, reduced by (dollars)` `the reduction` (`the total of` `the reduction`)

-- s 575(1)-(4) for one person, one parcel of land and one rating year.
GIVEN `the person`          IS A `Commonwealth payments and card`
      `the occupation`      IS AN `Occupation of the land`
      `the liability`       IS A `Liability for the rates`
      `the rates`           IS A `Rates and charges levied for the year`
      `the rating year`     IS A NUMBER
      `the levy day`        IS A DATE
      `the day of becoming an eligible pensioner` IS A DATE
      `the relief`          IS A `Council relief and regulations`
GIVETH A `Reduction answer`
`the s 575 reduction for` `the person` `the occupation` `the liability` `the rates` `the rating year` `the levy day` `the day of becoming an eligible pensioner` `the relief` MEANS
    IF `the relief`'s `a regulation under s 580 varies the amounts`
    THEN `not covered` `a regulation under s 580 varies the amounts of the reduction; the deposited regulation varies none`
    ELSE IF `the relief`'s `a council hardship order under s 577 applies`
         THEN `not covered` `a council hardship order under ss 577 and 578 applies; its effect and date are the council's`
         ELSE IF `the relief`'s `a council waiver or reduction under s 582 applies`
              THEN `not covered` `a council waiver or reduction under s 582 and cl 136 applies; its amount is the council's`
              ELSE IF NOT (`says eligible pensioner` `the status`)
                   THEN `no reduction: not an eligible pensioner` `the status`
                   ELSE IF     `the paragraph` EQUALS `s 575(2)(b): jointly liable with a person who is not a jointly eligible occupier -- the proportional share of one-half`
                           AND NOT (`the stated part is a part of the whole` `the liability`)
                        THEN `not covered` `the part stated for the applicant and jointly eligible occupiers is not more than 0 and at most 1`
                        ELSE CONSIDER `the position`
                             WHEN `not covered: the rates notice was not served in the rating year it is for (s 546(2), (3))` THEN `not covered` `the rates notice was not served in the rating year it is for (s 546(2), (3))`
                             WHEN `the whole year: an eligible pensioner on the day the rate or charge was levied (s 575(2))` THEN `reduced by` `the full reduction`
                             WHEN `full quarters remaining after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))` `q` THEN
                                 IF `q` EQUALS 0
                                 THEN `no reduction this year: no full quarter of the rating year remained after becoming an eligible pensioner (s 575(4))`
                                 ELSE `reduced by` (`the full reduction` `scaled by` (`q` DIVIDED BY `the number of quarters in a year`))
    WHERE
        `the status`         MEANS `the eligible pensioner status of` `the person` `on` `the occupation`
        `the paragraph`      MEANS `the s 575(2) paragraph for` `the liability`
        `the position`       MEANS `the s 575(4) position for` `the rating year` `levied on` `the levy day` `eligible from` `the day of becoming an eligible pensioner`
        `the full reduction` MEANS `the s 575(2) and (3) reduction of` `the rates` `at` (`the s 575(2) proportion for` `the liability`)

§§ `s 575(5) -- discharge as between persons jointly liable`

-- s 575(5): "A person who is an eligible pensioner or a jointly eligible occupier is, to the extent to which any rate
-- or charge that, but for this section, would be payable by the person is reduced under this section, discharged
-- from liability as between that person and any other person jointly liable to pay the rate or charge."
-- The amount the other persons jointly liable cannot ask the pensioner (and any jointly eligible occupier) to
-- contribute: the reduction, where anyone else is jointly liable; nothing to discharge where the pensioner is solely
-- liable.
GIVEN `the liability`       IS A `Liability for the rates`
      `the total reduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 575(5) discharge for` `the liability` `of` `the total reduction` MEANS
    IF `is jointly liable` `the liability`
    THEN `the total reduction`
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 584 -- ending of the concession`

-- s 584(1): "If circumstances occur that cause a person's entitlement to a reduction, under this Division, of rates
-- or charges to cease, the entitlement is taken to cease on the last day of the quarterly instalment period during
-- which those circumstances occur." READING (finding 5): "quarterly instalment period" is not defined; it is read as
-- the Dictionary "quarter" (cl 127(1)(j): "concessions are available to eligible pensioners for any quarter in which
-- they are eligible pensioners").
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the entitlement ceases after a change on` `the day of the change` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day of the change` AT LEAST 10
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 (DATE_YEAR `the day of the change`)
    ELSE IF DATE_MONTH `the day of the change` AT LEAST 7
         THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 30 9 (DATE_YEAR `the day of the change`)
         ELSE IF DATE_MONTH `the day of the change` AT LEAST 4
              THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 (DATE_YEAR `the day of the change`)
              ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 (DATE_YEAR `the day of the change`)

-- The quarterly instalment periods of the year remaining after the entitlement ceases.
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the quarterly instalment periods remaining after a change on` `the day of the change` MEANS
    `the number of full quarters of` (`the rating year containing` `the day of the change`) `remaining after` (`the day the entitlement ceases after a change on` `the day of the change`)

-- s 584(2): "If, at the time the entitlement is taken to cease, the rates or charges for the whole year, reduced under
-- this Division, have been paid in full, the portion of the payment that is proportionate to the quarterly instalment
-- periods remaining after that time is to be credited to the rates or charges payable in respect of that part of the
-- year remaining after that time."
DECLARE `Credit answer` IS ONE OF
    `credited to the rates and charges for the rest of the year (s 584(2)), in dollars` HAS `the credit` IS A NUMBER
    `no s 584(2) credit: the year's reduced rates and charges had not been paid in full when the entitlement ceased`

GIVEN `the day of the change`  IS A DATE
      `paid in full`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment`            IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Credit answer`
`the s 584(2) credit after a change on` `the day of the change` `paid in full` `the payment` MEANS
    IF `paid in full`
    THEN `credited to the rates and charges for the rest of the year (s 584(2)), in dollars` ((`the payment` TIMES (`the quarterly instalment periods remaining after a change on` `the day of the change`)) DIVIDED BY `the number of quarters in a year`)
    ELSE `no s 584(2) credit: the year's reduced rates and charges had not been paid in full when the entitlement ceased`

§§ `s 583 -- writing off, and when the council may recover`

-- s 583(1): "A council is to write off amounts of rates, charges and interest which are reduced or waived under this
-- Division." (2): "A council may not take proceedings to recover an amount so written off unless the amount has been
-- written off because of a wilfully false statement in an application under this Division or except as provided by
-- section 584." READING (finding 6): s 584 grants no power to recover in terms; the exception is read as reaching an
-- amount written off for a period after the entitlement ceased under s 584(1).
GIVEN `written off because of a wilfully false statement in the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `written off for a period after the entitlement ceased under s 584`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the council may take proceedings to recover the amount written off` `written off because of a wilfully false statement in the application` `written off for a period after the entitlement ceased under s 584` IF
        `written off because of a wilfully false statement in the application`
    OR  `written off for a period after the entitlement ceased under s 584`

§§ `s 582 and cl 136 -- who the council may choose to relieve`

-- s 582: "A council may waive or reduce rates, charges and interest due by any person prescribed by the regulations who
-- is in receipt of a pension, benefit or allowance under the Social Security Act 1991 of the Commonwealth." cl 136:
-- "any person who receives a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991 of the
-- Commonwealth and is the holder of a pensioner concession card issued by or on behalf of the Commonwealth Government
-- is a prescribed person." Holding the card, not entitlement to it (cl 134(a)); a VEA service pension alone is not
-- enough (finding 8). Whether and how much the council waives is its discretion: not covered.
GIVEN `receives a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the holder of a pensioner concession card`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a person prescribed by cl 136` `receives a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991` `is the holder of a pensioner concession card` IF
        `receives a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991`
    AND `is the holder of a pensioner concession card`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the eligible pensioner and the council`

-- Clock: days. Day 0 is the day the rule starts, as each rule says.
DECLARE `Concession party` IS ONE OF `the eligible pensioner`, `the council`

DECLARE `Concession act` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the council in the approved form, with evidence enough to calculate the reduction`
    `reduce the rate or charge`
    `write off the amount reduced`
    `take proceedings to recover the amount written off`
    `credit the prepaid portion to the rest of the year` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `reduce a later rate or charge without a further application`
    `waive or reduce rates, charges and interest`

-- s 575(1): the rate or charge "is, on application to the council and on production to the council of evidence
-- sufficient to enable it to calculate the amount of the reduction, to be reduced". s 579(1): "An application under
-- this Division is to be made within the time and in the manner prescribed by the regulations." cl 135: "An
-- application ... is to be made in the form approved by the Secretary." The regulation prescribes the manner but no
-- time, so the time is the one "fixed by resolution of the council" (s 579(2); finding 7): an input, NOTHING if the
-- resolution fixes none. s 583(1): the council "is to write off" the amounts reduced. Applying is the pensioner's
-- choice: not applying is no breach (DO ... LEST FULFILLED), but brings no reduction. The Act sets the council no
-- period. Day 0: the day the rates notice is served.
GIVEN `is an eligible pensioner liable for the rate or charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days fixed by council resolution for applying`      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Concession party` `Concession act`
DECIDE `s 575(1), 579, 583(1) -- on the pensioner's application, the council must reduce the rate or charge and write the reduction off` IS
    IF NOT `is an eligible pensioner liable for the rate or charge`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE CONSIDER `the days fixed by council resolution for applying`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             PARTY `the eligible pensioner`
             DO    `apply to the council in the approved form, with evidence enough to calculate the reduction`
             HENCE `the council's duties on an application`
             LEST  FULFILLED
         WHEN JUST `days` THEN
             PARTY `the eligible pensioner`
             DO    `apply to the council in the approved form, with evidence enough to calculate the reduction`
             WITHIN `days`
             HENCE `the council's duties on an application`
             LEST  FULFILLED
    WHERE
        `the council's duties on an application` MEANS
                (PARTY `the council`
                 MUST  `reduce the rate or charge`
                 LEST  BREACH BY `the council` BECAUSE "s 575(1): on application and evidence, the rate or charge of an eligible pensioner is to be reduced")
            RAND
                (PARTY `the council`
                 MUST  `write off the amount reduced`
                 LEST  BREACH BY `the council` BECAUSE "s 583(1): a council is to write off amounts of rates and charges reduced under Division 1")

-- s 583(2): the council "may not take proceedings to recover an amount so written off unless" a wilfully false
-- statement, or s 584. The prohibition has no end in the Act; the rule runs for the number of days asked about.
-- Day 0: the day the amount is written off.
GIVEN `written off because of a wilfully false statement in the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `written off for a period after the entitlement ceased under s 584`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days asked about`                                                 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Concession party` `Concession act`
DECIDE `s 583(2) -- the council must not take proceedings to recover an amount written off, unless for a false statement or under s 584` IS
    IF `the council may take proceedings to recover the amount written off` `written off because of a wilfully false statement in the application` `written off for a period after the entitlement ceased under s 584`
    THEN PARTY `the council`
         MAY   `take proceedings to recover the amount written off`
    ELSE PARTY `the council`
         SHANT `take proceedings to recover the amount written off`
         WITHIN `the days asked about`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the council` BECAUSE "s 583(2): a council may not take proceedings to recover a pensioner reduction it has written off, unless for a wilfully false statement or as s 584 provides"

-- s 584(2): the portion "is to be credited to the rates or charges payable in respect of that part of the year
-- remaining". No period is stated. Day 0: the day the entitlement ceases.
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE
      `paid in full`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment`           IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Concession party` `Concession act`
DECIDE `s 584(2) -- the council must credit the prepaid portion when the concession ends` IS
    CONSIDER `the s 584(2) credit after a change on` `the day of the change` `paid in full` `the payment`
    WHEN `credited to the rates and charges for the rest of the year (s 584(2)), in dollars` `the credit` THEN
        PARTY `the council`
        MUST  `credit the prepaid portion to the rest of the year` (EXACTLY `the credit`)
        LEST  BREACH BY `the council` BECAUSE "s 584(2): the portion of a full payment for the quarterly instalment periods remaining is to be credited"
    WHEN `no s 584(2) credit: the year's reduced rates and charges had not been paid in full when the entitlement ceased` THEN FULFILLED

-- s 579(3): "If, pursuant to an application made under this Division, a reduced rate or charge applies, the council
-- may, if the eligibility of the applicant for a reduction in a subsequent rate or charge is verified by the council
-- as prescribed by the regulations, reduce the subsequent rate or charge without requiring a further application." A
-- permission. The deposited regulation prescribes no way of verifying (finding 7): whether it was verified "as
-- prescribed" is an input.
GIVEN `a reduced rate applies on an earlier application`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `eligibility verified by the council as prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Concession party` `Concession act`
DECIDE `s 579(3) -- the council may reduce a later rate or charge without a further application` IS
    IF `a reduced rate applies on an earlier application` AND `eligibility verified by the council as prescribed`
    THEN PARTY `the council`
         MAY   `reduce a later rate or charge without a further application`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 582 with cl 136: the council "may waive or reduce" the rates of a prescribed person. A permission; for anyone else
-- s 582 gives none, and nothing is owed (FULFILLED).
GIVEN `receives a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is the holder of a pensioner concession card`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Concession party` `Concession act`
DECIDE `s 582 -- the council may waive or reduce the rates of a person prescribed by cl 136` IS
    IF `is a person prescribed by cl 136` `receives a pension, benefit or allowance under Chapter 2 of the Social Security Act 1991` `is the holder of a pensioner concession card`
    THEN PARTY `the council`
         MAY   `waive or reduce rates, charges and interest`
    ELSE FULFILLED
